  :adr/body
  "## The pattern

**A default or fallback endpoint the workspace does not authoritatively own, on
a code path that transmits a credential.**

Found first in `etzhayyim/root`, where a CLI defaulted its PDS host to
`https://pds.local`. `.local` is the mDNS/Bonjour namespace (RFC 6762), so the
name is claimable by **any host on the same link** -- and that command sends
`Authorization: Bearer $E7M_TOKEN` to whatever answered first. On a shared
network it hands a bearer token to whoever replies fastest.

That is arguably worse than the ambient env read a previous fix removed, since
an env read at least required someone to set something.

## Sweep result: it was not the three sites we knew about

Six independent lenses over 4,149 checked-out repos. **Three genuinely new
instances**, and the worst of them is worse than two of the three we started
from.

| rank | site | default | credential | state |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `kotoba-lang/sdk-py` `llm.cljc:22` | `http://levi.local:4000` | **`Bearer $ETZHAYYIM_LLM_KEY`** | **unfixed at sweep time** |
| 2 | `etzhayyim/root` `yoroshiku.cljc` | `https://pds.local` | `$E7M_TOKEN` | fixed |
| 3 | `kotoba-lang/vpn` `peer_manager.py:10` | `http://TODO_EXIT_NODE_IP:8081` | shared secret + WireGuard peer keys | **unfixed at sweep time** |
| 4 | `etzhayyim/root` `murakumo_cmd.py:579` | `http://benjamin.local:4646` | conditional -- inherits full environ | open |
| 5 | `kotoba-lang/sdk-py` `mst_projector.cljc:19` | `http://simeon.local:8765` | none | **unfixed at sweep time** |
| 6 | `etzhayyim/root` `xrpc.cljc:243` | `https://pds.local` | none | fixed since |
| 7 | `etzhayyim/root` `training.cljc:280` | `https://pds.local` | none -- never sends | fixed since |

Fixes for 1, 3 and 5 are in flight; 6 and 7 landed as `be9c1b1a2cf`.

## Two things the ranking teaches, which the pattern alone does not

**Same shape, different severity.** Of the three original sites, only ONE
transmitted a credential. `xrpc` sends but unauthenticated -- it leaks the
payload and the NSID. `training` never sends at all: every branch ends in a
print, so it merely displayed a plan naming a squattable host. Calling all three
a security defect would have been wrong, and the commits say which each is.

**Severity is not proportional to how alarming the string looks.** The
`TODO_EXIT_NODE_IP` placeholder reads worse than `levi.local` and is probably
less exploitable: the underscore makes most resolvers reject the label outright,
so it fails CLOSED, while a well-formed mDNS name fails OPEN into an attacker's
hands. **An unresolvable wrong default is safer than a resolvable one** -- which
is why the honest fix for a placeholder is usually to require the value and fail
loudly, not to invent a host to fall back to.

## What is NOT this pattern

Reported explicitly so the list stays readable and so nobody re-investigates:

- **`*.svc.cluster.local`** (~1,100 hits) -- reserved Kubernetes cluster domain,
  authoritative in-cluster.
- **Cloudflare service-binding / Durable Object URLs** (`assets.local`,
  `https://auth.internal/...`) -- the hostname is a required-but-ignored
  placeholder that never touches DNS.
- **`localhost` / `127.0.0.1` for co-located sidecars** (~60 sites: Ollama,
  VOICEVOX, ComfyUI, LiteLLM, Kubo). `localhost` is the CORRECT default for a
  sidecar and is not attacker-claimable.
- **`0.0.0.0`** -- all hits are bind addresses, none a client target.
- Test fixtures, and scraped third-party corpora (651 `test.pds.local` are
  harvested PDS endpoints, not code -- re-scanned outside the data directories
  to confirm the exclusion hid nothing).

## The Python originals were already right

`training.py` computes `(pds or resolve_pds())` in every subcommand and
`xrpc.py` resolves through `auth.resolve_pds()`. The `.cljc` ports substituted a
literal at both sites. **This class entered through porting, not through
design** -- which suggests looking at other ports before looking for a policy
failure.

## Coverage gap, stated rather than buried

**266 of 4,165 west-registered repos (6.4%) are not on disk and were not
scanned.** Verified genuinely absent, not path-mismatched. The set is heavily
`cloud-itonami/actor-*` and `cloud-itonami/app-*` -- **which is the concerning
shape**, because per the `build-actor` pattern those repos authenticate to
`kotobase.net` with self-minted CACAO. `repo-search.cljs` matches names and
READMEs, not source bodies, so it cannot close this; it needs `west update` on
that group.

Also undetermined: whether site 4 is live depends on whether `NOMAD_TOKEN` is
set in a real operator environment, which is not answerable from the tree.

## Method notes worth keeping

- **The syntax-independent lens found all three known instances; the
  pattern-shaped lens found one.** Searching for `.local` URLs outright beat
  searching for the env-read-with-fallback IDIOM, because the same defect is
  written several ways. When checking whether a search is broad enough, prefer
  the lens that does not encode a guess about how the code is spelled.
- **A first regex truncated real domains at the first dot** and produced 2.3M
  garbage hits (`https://pds` out of `pds.example.com`). Rewritten with a
  terminator lookahead. A search that returns millions of hits is not thorough;
  it is broken.
- **Working trees were scanned, and nothing was fetched.** `orgs/etzhayyim/root`
  is 6,695 commits behind its `origin/main`, so two of its three sites were read
  as unfixed from the tree while one was already fixed on main. Which tree was
  read is recorded per finding, because `main`, the pin, and the checkout are
  three different things."}]
